VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id
# NOTE: Gemini and ElevenLabs API keys are server-side only (consumed by
# their respective Supabase Edge Functions) — never add VITE_-prefixed
# entries for them here. A VITE_-prefixed var gets bundled into the client
# and is publicly readable; that's exactly how a prior RevenueCat secret
# key leaked into the app bundle. Set GEMINI_API_KEY / ELEVENLABS_API_KEY
# as edge function secrets instead (`supabase secrets set`).
# Full inventory of every secret this app uses (server-side and client-side,
# with a note on which are meant to be public): docs/secrets-inventory.md

# In-app purchases (RevenueCat) — these are RevenueCat's own *public* API
# keys, meant for client embedding (distinct from REVENUECAT_SECRET_KEY,
# which is server-side only, an edge function secret, never here)
VITE_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=goog_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
VITE_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=appl_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Error monitoring (Sentry) — leave blank in dev to disable
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0
# NOTE: VITE_APP_VERSION here does nothing — vite.config.ts's `define` block
# always overwrites import.meta.env.VITE_APP_VERSION with package.json's
# version at build time, regardless of what's set in the environment. Kept
# out of this file so it doesn't imply this var is configurable; see
# src/pages/settings/DiagnosticsPage.tsx for where the real version surfaces.

# Analytics (PostHog) — leave blank in dev to disable
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://app.posthog.com
